turns.assistant:
For a portfolio contact form, it's a nice touch but not essential. Most people send one message.

If you want it, it's simple:

```jsx
if (status === 'sent') {
  return (
    <div>
      <p>Thanks! I'll be in touch.</p>
      <button onClick={() => { setForm({ name: '', email: '', message: '' }); setStatus('idle'); }}>
        Send another message
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

I'd make it a text link style rather than a big button, so it doesn't compete with the confirmation message. Also consider moving focus to the success message when it appears, so keyboard and screen reader users know the form was submitted.
